cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "What Actually Matters at 10M Parameters? A Preregistered Ablation Study of Small Transformer Language Models"
authors:
  - family-names: Detroja
    given-names: Vraj
version: 1.0.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/vrajdetroja/micro-lm-ablations"
abstract: >-
  A preregistered, controlled ablation study of 10M-parameter transformer language
  models. It compares 24 architecture, initialization, schedule, tokenizer, and
  optimizer variants against a GPT-2-style baseline, each at its own best learning
  rate, matched on parameters and tokens, and judged against a measured noise floor.
keywords:
  - language models
  - transformers
  - ablation study
  - preregistration
  - scaling laws
